' craft-bridge probe-primorient - Phase 1 batch 3 PRIMITIVE ORIENTATION
' PROBE: what the primitive path does on this seat. Four cases in fresh
' parts, each drawing the emitter's generated profile at the MAPPED
' coordinates of a fixed source-space footprint (the 2x2 map computed from
' the probed source-XY plane frame exactly as the emitter's PublishMap
' computes and stores it):
'
'   box-dir-false / box-dir-true: the mapped box (four lines in the
'   emitter's deterministic order, ln0 the SC-u edge = the length edge)
'   with the emitter's two size dimensions, blindly extruded 0.012 m with
'   the emitter's exact 23-argument call shape and the case's Dir flag.
'   Each case reports the probed frame, the computed map entries and side,
'   each created dimension's Name and SystemValue WITH ITS SIGN, the D1
'   identity and SystemValue, and IPartDoc.GetPartBox(True) with every
'   component.
'
'   cylinder-dim: the mapped circle (the emitter's CreateCircleByRadius
'   call) anchored like the emitter's, with the circle dimension created
'   exactly as the emitter creates it - the report carries the created
'   value against GetRadius AND twice it, which is the radius-kind vs
'   diameter-kind pin for primitive sizes and sketch radius dimensions
'   alike - then the emitter's kind guards, and only if they pass the same
'   blind extrusion and box.
'
'   box-edit-follow: the mapped box with the emitter's whole shape
'   contract (coincident corners, classified horizontal/vertical
'   relations, the corner fix) and its two size dimensions, then a
'   parameter change - the length dimension driven to 1.5x its drawn
'   value - with a full corner readback (every endpoint coordinate, both
'   edge lengths, the closure). No feature is created.
'
' Reading the pin - kept narrow on purpose (the plan review's scope
' bound): the two box cases pin which physical side the Dir flag sends
' the primitive's height to, ON THIS SEAT'S SOURCE-XY CONFIGURATION (the
' positive-normal reading), and cross-check probe-extrudedir's
' TT_EX_DIR_TRUE_SIDE reading on a second frame that carries a
' non-identity map. Two candidate frame laws remain open: the flag follows
' the transform-reported sketch normal, or a host-canonicalized normal.
' These cases cannot distinguish the two wherever they agree - they agree
' whenever the transform normal IS the canonical one, as on the
' positive-normal planes here - so a matching result confirms the
' emitter's composition for the measured configuration ONLY and never
' proves the general law; a mismatch with the Front-plane reading refutes
' frame-relativity and must stop the fill-in. The opposing-normal
' composition (map side -1) is not covered by any case here (every origin
' plane on this seat publishes a permutation map with side +1) and stays
' an accepted residual under the seat-acceptance outer guard. Filling
' TT_PRIM_DIR_TRUE_SIDE from these reports is evidence for the measured
' configuration only - never proof of the reflected case. GetPartBox is
' approximate per its documentation, so sides are read with tolerance,
' never by exact endpoint equality. The probe reports the numbers; it
' draws no conclusion the box does not carry.
'
' Evidence discipline: every SolidWorks API call captures its numeric
' error and description at its own named stage (the host-file report
' plumbing - path discovery, open/append - is the proven helper set and
' suppresses its own I/O errors by design); entering records precede the
' risky calls (feature creation, AddDimension2, GetPartBox); contexts are
' verified before the named measurements and re-verified after the
' mutating feature call (with selections cleared and checked); missing
' setup geometry fails the run with a failed step while cleanup still
' runs. Procedure bodies run under captured-error discipline: a raised
' call error is captured at its own named stage before any failure path,
' and every numeric value is rejected if Empty/Null/nonnumeric before
' conversion - nothing is silently coerced or defaulted. The map
' computation is fail-closed exactly like the emitter's PublishMap: the
' 16-entry transform form, finite entries, scale 1, unit axes, mutual
' orthogonality and the right-handed 3D frame must all hold before a
' single entry is used. Required observations: the map entries and side,
' every created dimension identity and value, the box form and all six
' components, and the D1 identity. Cleanup is tri-state and
' ownership-checked on every path (close/keep/unknown); authorization is
' established before any model creation; a keep-mode handoff must verify
' as a live, nonempty, uniquely owned document or the run fails and the
' document is closed instead. Setup failure aborts the remaining cases; a
' measurement failure fails the run but lets the independent remaining
' cases record their own evidence (fresh parts, no shared state).
' Diagnostic instrument, not a fidelity golden.
Option Explicit

Dim swApp As SldWorks.SldWorks
Dim swDoc As SldWorks.ModelDoc2
Dim swSketchMgr As SketchManager
Dim reportPath As String
Dim gProbeLog As String
Dim gTemplate As String
Dim gFeatMgr As Object
Dim gRunFailed As Boolean
Dim gDimToggle As Boolean
Dim gDimToggleSaved As Boolean
' The per-case adaptation map, computed from the probed frame exactly as
' the emitter's PublishMap stores it: s = u*gMap00 + v*gMap10, t =
' u*gMap01 + v*gMap11, gMapSide = sign(n_sk . source +Z).
Dim gMap00 As Double
Dim gMap01 As Double
Dim gMap10 As Double
Dim gMap11 As Double
Dim gMapSide As Long

Sub main()
    Dim mode As String
    Dim r As Long
    Dim closedOk As Boolean
    Dim errNum As Long
    Dim errMsg As String
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error GoTo Fail
    gRunFailed = False
    reportPath = ReportPathFromHost()
    If reportPath = "" Then Err.Raise vbObjectError + 513, "probe-primorient", "no report path"
    StartReport
    WriteLine "{""type"":""header"",""macro"":""probe-primorient"",""bridge_version"":""0.1.0""}"
    mode = CloseMode()
    If mode = "unknown" Then
        WriteStep -1, "close-mode", "failed", "cleanup authorization is not established; no model is created"
        gRunFailed = True
        GoTo WrapUp
    End If
    On Error Resume Next
    Err.Clear
    Set swApp = Application.SldWorks
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    On Error GoTo Fail
    WriteLine LineFor("application", n, d, "stage=acquire")
    If n <> 0 Or swApp Is Nothing Then Err.Raise vbObjectError + 516, "probe-primorient", "the SolidWorks application could not be acquired"
    ' The input-dimension-value dialog blocks AddDimension2 (minimal.swb):
    ' save the owner's value, disable, verify the disable; every exit
    ' restores the SAVED value and verifies the restore - never force one.
    gDimToggle = swApp.GetUserPreferenceToggle(swUserPreferenceToggle_e.swInputDimValOnCreate)
    gDimToggleSaved = True
    swApp.SetUserPreferenceToggle swUserPreferenceToggle_e.swInputDimValOnCreate, False
    If swApp.GetUserPreferenceToggle(swUserPreferenceToggle_e.swInputDimValOnCreate) Then Err.Raise vbObjectError + 528, "probe-primorient", "the input-dimension-value dialog could not be disabled"
    On Error Resume Next
    Err.Clear
    gTemplate = swApp.GetUserPreferenceStringValue(swUserPreferenceStringValue_e.swDefaultTemplatePart)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    On Error GoTo Fail
    WriteLine LineFor("template", n, d, "stage=default-part-template value=" & gTemplate)
    If n <> 0 Then Err.Raise vbObjectError + 514, "probe-primorient", "the default part template could not be read"
    If gTemplate = "" Then Err.Raise vbObjectError + 514, "probe-primorient", "no default part template is configured"
    r = RunBoxCase("box-dir-false", False, False, mode)
    If r <> 0 Then gRunFailed = True
    If r >= 2 Then GoTo WrapUp
    Err.Clear
    mode = CloseMode()
    If mode = "unknown" Then
        WriteStep -1, "close-mode", "failed", "cleanup authorization lost; no further case is started"
        gRunFailed = True
        GoTo WrapUp
    End If
    r = RunBoxCase("box-dir-true", True, False, mode)
    If r <> 0 Then gRunFailed = True
    If r >= 2 Then GoTo WrapUp
    Err.Clear
    mode = CloseMode()
    If mode = "unknown" Then
        WriteStep -1, "close-mode", "failed", "cleanup authorization lost; no further case is started"
        gRunFailed = True
        GoTo WrapUp
    End If
    r = RunCylinderCase("cylinder-dim", False, mode)
    If r <> 0 Then gRunFailed = True
    If r >= 2 Then GoTo WrapUp
    Err.Clear
    mode = CloseMode()
    If mode = "unknown" Then
        WriteStep -1, "close-mode", "failed", "cleanup authorization lost; no further case is started"
        gRunFailed = True
        GoTo WrapUp
    End If
    r = RunEditCase("box-edit-follow", True, mode)
    If r <> 0 Then gRunFailed = True
    If r >= 2 Then GoTo WrapUp
WrapUp:
    If gDimToggleSaved And Not swApp Is Nothing Then
        swApp.SetUserPreferenceToggle swUserPreferenceToggle_e.swInputDimValOnCreate, gDimToggle
        If swApp.GetUserPreferenceToggle(swUserPreferenceToggle_e.swInputDimValOnCreate) <> gDimToggle Then WriteStep -1, "toggle-restore", "failed", "the input-dimension-value preference did not restore"
    End If
    If gRunFailed Then
        WriteLine "{""type"":""summary"",""status"":""failed""}"
    Else
        WriteLine "{""type"":""summary"",""status"":""ok""}"
    End If
    Exit Sub
Fail:
    errNum = Err.Number
    errMsg = Err.Description
    On Error Resume Next
    WriteLine "{""type"":""step"",""index"":-1,""command"":""probe"",""status"":""failed"",""message"":""" & JsonStr("err " & Trim(Str(errNum)) & ": " & errMsg) & """}"
    If gDimToggleSaved And Not swApp Is Nothing Then
        swApp.SetUserPreferenceToggle swUserPreferenceToggle_e.swInputDimValOnCreate, gDimToggle
        If swApp.GetUserPreferenceToggle(swUserPreferenceToggle_e.swInputDimValOnCreate) <> gDimToggle Then WriteStep -1, "toggle-restore", "failed", "the input-dimension-value preference did not restore on the failure path"
    End If
    If Not swDoc Is Nothing Then
        CloseOwnedDoc closedOk
        If Not closedOk Then WriteStep -1, "close", "failed", "the owned document could not be confirmed closed"
    End If
    WriteLine "{""type"":""summary"",""status"":""failed""}"
End Sub

' One box orientation case: fresh part, the source-XY plane opened exactly
' as the emitter's OpenSketchOnPlane accepts it (the geometric plane), the
' adaptation map computed fail-closed from the probed frame, the emitter's
' mapped box drawing and size dimensions, then the emitter's blind
' extrusion call shape with the case's Dir flag and the box/dimension
' evidence. Returns 0 = complete, 1 = measurement failure (the run is
' failed; later independent cases still record), 2 = setup failure (the
' run is failed and the remaining cases are aborted), 3 = the case's
' document could not be confirmed closed or handed off (the run is failed
' and the remaining cases are aborted). Cleanup runs on every path; only
' the final case may be kept open, then only in keep mode and only after
' its handoff verifies live.
Function RunBoxCase(ByVal tag As String, ByVal dirFlag As Boolean, ByVal isFinal As Boolean, ByVal mode As String) As Long
    Dim result As Long
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim verified As Boolean
    Dim measOk As Boolean
    Dim nameOk As Boolean
    Dim feat As Object
    Dim extSel As Object
    Dim featName As String
    Dim featShown As String
    Dim skName As String
    Dim handoffTitle As String
    Dim closedOk As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    Dim ln0 As Object
    Dim ln1 As Object
    Dim ln2 As Object
    Dim ln3 As Object
    Dim dmLen As Object
    Dim dmWid As Object
    On Error Resume Next
    result = 2
    WriteLine LineFor("case-" & tag, 0, "", "entering: mapped box SC u 0.010..0.050 v 0.020..0.035 (metres), blind 0.012 m, Dir=" & CStr(dirFlag))
    Err.Clear
    Set swDoc = swApp.NewDocument(gTemplate, 0, 0, 0)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("document.new-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or swDoc Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep -1, "document.new", "failed", "the fresh part for " & tag & " could not be created"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    Set swSketchMgr = swDoc.SketchManager
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sketchmgr-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or swSketchMgr Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep -1, "sketchmgr", "failed", "no sketch manager for " & tag
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    Set gFeatMgr = swDoc.FeatureManager
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("featuremgr-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or gFeatMgr Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep -1, "featuremgr", "failed", "no feature manager for " & tag
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    If Not OpenSketchOnPlaneXY(skName) Then
        WriteStep 0, "sketch.open", "failed", "no plane carries the source-XY geometric frame (translation at the model origin, normal parallel to +Z); probed: " & gProbeLog & "; tree scan saw: " & TreeSummary()
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 0, "sketch.open", "created", gProbeLog & "sketch feature " & skName
    If Not ComputeMap() Then
        WriteStep 0, "map", "failed", "the adaptation map could not be computed fail-closed from the probed frame; the case is refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 0, "map", "created", "m00=" & Trim(Str(gMap00)) & " m01=" & Trim(Str(gMap01)) & " m10=" & Trim(Str(gMap10)) & " m11=" & Trim(Str(gMap11)) & " side=" & Trim(Str(gMapSide)) & " frame " & FrameTextEx()
    ReportContext "active", verified
    If Not verified Then
        WriteStep 1, "context", "failed", "the active-sketch context is not verified"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Set ln0 = MappedLine(tag, 1, 0.01, 0.02, 0.05, 0.02)
    Set ln1 = MappedLine(tag, 2, 0.05, 0.02, 0.05, 0.035)
    Set ln2 = MappedLine(tag, 3, 0.05, 0.035, 0.01, 0.035)
    Set ln3 = MappedLine(tag, 4, 0.01, 0.035, 0.01, 0.02)
    If ln0 Is Nothing Or ln1 Is Nothing Or ln2 Is Nothing Or ln3 Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep 2, "profile", "failed", "the mapped box profile is incomplete; the direction pin is refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 2, "profile", "created", "four mapped lines at the mapped corners of SC u 0.010..0.050 v 0.020..0.035 (ln0 = the u edge = the length edge)"
    If Not SizeDim(tag & "-length", ln0, 0.04, dmLen) Then
        WriteStep 2, "dim-length", "failed", "the length dimension evidence is incomplete"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    If Not SizeDim(tag & "-width", ln1, 0.015, dmWid) Then
        WriteStep 2, "dim-width", "failed", "the width dimension evidence is incomplete"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 2, "dims", "created", "the length and width dimensions were created with sign-resolved values (see the sizedim records)"
    Err.Clear
    swSketchMgr.InsertSketch True
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sketch.close-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteStep 1, "context", "failed", "the sketch could not be closed"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    ReportContext "closed", verified
    If Not verified Then
        WriteStep 1, "context", "failed", "the closed-sketch context is not verified; the feature call is refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.ClearSelection2 True
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("clearselection-" & tag, n, d, "stage=preselect")
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteStep 1, "selection", "failed", "selections could not be cleared before selecting the profile"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    Set extSel = swDoc.Extension
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("selectsketch-" & tag, n, d, "stage=extension-acquire")
    If n <> 0 Or extSel Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep 3, "extrude", "failed", "the Extension could not be acquired; the profile sketch cannot be selected"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    ok = extSel.SelectByID2(skName, "SKETCH", 0#, 0#, 0#, False, 0, Nothing, swSelectOption_e.swSelectOptionDefault)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("selectsketch-" & tag, n, d, "stage=selectbyname name=" & skName & " result=" & CStr(ok))
    If n <> 0 Or Not ok Then
        WriteStep 3, "extrude", "failed", "the profile sketch " & skName & " could not be selected; the extrusion is not attempted (setup)"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    result = 1
    WriteLine LineFor("featureextrusion2-" & tag, 0, "", "entering: FeatureExtrusion2(True, False, " & CStr(dirFlag) & ", swEndCondBlind, swEndCondBlind, 0.012, 0#, False, False, False, False, 0#, 0#, False, False, False, False, True, True, True, 0, 0#, False)")
    Err.Clear
    Set feat = gFeatMgr.FeatureExtrusion2(True, False, dirFlag, swEndConditions_e.swEndCondBlind, swEndConditions_e.swEndCondBlind, 0.012, 0#, False, False, False, False, 0#, 0#, False, False, False, False, True, True, True, 0, 0#, False)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("featureextrusion2-" & tag, n, d, "outcome")
    If n <> 0 Or feat Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep 3, "extrude", "failed", "the blind extrusion (Dir=" & CStr(dirFlag) & ") was not created; direction evidence is incomplete"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    featName = feat.Name
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("feature-name-" & tag, n, d, "name=" & featName)
    nameOk = True
    featShown = featName
    If n <> 0 Or Trim(featName) = "" Then
        nameOk = False
        featShown = "(name unavailable)"
        WriteLine LineFor("feature-name-" & tag, -1, "name unavailable", "the D1 lookup cannot be constructed; its key is never issued empty")
    End If
    WriteStep 3, "extrude", "created", "blind 0.012 m, Dir=" & CStr(dirFlag) & ", feature " & featShown
    ReportContext "closed", verified
    If Not verified Then
        WriteStep 4, "measure-" & tag, "failed", "the post-feature context is not verified; measurements are refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.ClearSelection2 True
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("clearselection-" & tag, n, d, "stage=premeasure")
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteStep 4, "measure-" & tag, "failed", "selections could not be cleared before the measurements"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    measOk = True
    BoxEvidence tag, ok
    If Not ok Then measOk = False
    If nameOk Then
        DimEvidence "dim-d1-" & tag, "D1@" & featName, True, ok
        If Not ok Then measOk = False
    Else
        WriteLine LineFor("dim-d1-" & tag, -1, "lookup unavailable", "required: no feature name; the D1 identity is missing")
        measOk = False
    End If
    If measOk Then
        WriteStep 4, "measure-" & tag, "created", "map entries and side captured; both size dimensions captured with sign; box form and all 6 components captured; D1 identity captured"
        result = 0
    Else
        WriteStep 4, "measure-" & tag, "failed", "a required observation is missing"
    End If
CaseCleanup:
    On Error Resume Next
    If isFinal And mode = "keep" Then
        ok = OwnedHandoffVerified(tag, handoffTitle)
        If ok Then
            WriteStep 5, "owned-document", "kept-open", handoffTitle
        Else
            WriteStep 5, "owned-document", "failed", "the keep-mode handoff is unverified; the document is not reported as retained"
            result = 3
            CloseOwnedDoc closedOk
            If Not closedOk Then WriteStep 5, "close", "failed", "the unverified handoff could not be confirmed closed"
        End If
    Else
        CloseOwnedDoc closedOk
        If Not closedOk Then
            WriteStep 5, "close", "failed", "the owned document could not be confirmed closed"
            result = 3
        End If
    End If
    Set swDoc = Nothing
    Set swSketchMgr = Nothing
    Set gFeatMgr = Nothing
    RunBoxCase = result
End Function

' The cylinder-kind case: the mapped circle anchored like the emitter's,
' the circle dimension created exactly as the emitter creates it (the
' created value reported against GetRadius and twice it - the radius-kind
' vs diameter-kind pin), then the emitter's kind guards and - only when
' they pass - the emitter's blind extrusion and the box evidence.
Function RunCylinderCase(ByVal tag As String, ByVal isFinal As Boolean, ByVal mode As String) As Long
    Dim result As Long
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim verified As Boolean
    Dim measOk As Boolean
    Dim nameOk As Boolean
    Dim kindOk As Boolean
    Dim feat As Object
    Dim extSel As Object
    Dim featName As String
    Dim featShown As String
    Dim skName As String
    Dim handoffTitle As String
    Dim closedOk As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    Dim ci As Object
    Dim pA As Object
    Dim dmRad As Object
    On Error Resume Next
    result = 2
    WriteLine LineFor("case-" & tag, 0, "", "entering: mapped circle SC base (0.023,-0.031) r 0.006 (metres), blind 0.012 m, Dir=False")
    Err.Clear
    Set swDoc = swApp.NewDocument(gTemplate, 0, 0, 0)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("document.new-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or swDoc Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep -1, "document.new", "failed", "the fresh part for " & tag & " could not be created"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    Set swSketchMgr = swDoc.SketchManager
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sketchmgr-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or swSketchMgr Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep -1, "sketchmgr", "failed", "no sketch manager for " & tag
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    Set gFeatMgr = swDoc.FeatureManager
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("featuremgr-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or gFeatMgr Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep -1, "featuremgr", "failed", "no feature manager for " & tag
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    If Not OpenSketchOnPlaneXY(skName) Then
        WriteStep 0, "sketch.open", "failed", "no plane carries the source-XY geometric frame (translation at the model origin, normal parallel to +Z); probed: " & gProbeLog & "; tree scan saw: " & TreeSummary()
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 0, "sketch.open", "created", gProbeLog & "sketch feature " & skName
    If Not ComputeMap() Then
        WriteStep 0, "map", "failed", "the adaptation map could not be computed fail-closed from the probed frame; the case is refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 0, "map", "created", "m00=" & Trim(Str(gMap00)) & " m01=" & Trim(Str(gMap01)) & " m10=" & Trim(Str(gMap10)) & " m11=" & Trim(Str(gMap11)) & " side=" & Trim(Str(gMapSide)) & " frame " & FrameTextEx()
    ReportContext "active", verified
    If Not verified Then
        WriteStep 1, "context", "failed", "the active-sketch context is not verified"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Set ci = MappedCircle(tag, 0.023, -0.031, 0.006)
    If ci Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep 2, "profile", "failed", "the mapped cylinder circle is missing; the kind pin is refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 2, "profile", "created", "mapped circle at the mapped centre of SC (0.023,-0.031), r 0.006"
    ' The emitter's centre anchor (sgFix on the GetCenterPoint2 handle).
    Err.Clear
    Set pA = ci.GetCenterPoint2
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("centre-handle-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or pA Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep 2, "anchor", "failed", "the cylinder centre handle is missing"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    ok = pA.Select(False)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("centre-fix-" & tag, n, d, "stage=select result=" & CStr(ok))
    If n <> 0 Or Not ok Then
        WriteStep 2, "anchor", "failed", "the cylinder centre anchor would not select"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.SketchAddConstraints "sgFix"
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("centre-fix-" & tag, n, d, "stage=sgFix (no return value; application is indistinguishable from a pre-held predicate at creation)")
    swDoc.ClearSelection2 True
    WriteStep 2, "anchor", "created", "sgFix applied on the centre point (behaviourally established by box-edit-follow's corner anchor, same vocabulary)"
    If Not CircleDim(tag, ci, 0.006, dmRad, kindOk) Then
        WriteStep 2, "circledim", "failed", "the circle dimension evidence is incomplete"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    If Not kindOk Then
        WriteStep 2, "circledim", "failed", "the circle-size dimension kind is not radius-kind or ambiguous; the emitter's guard refuses exactly this (the report carries the numbers)"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 2, "circledim", "created", "the circle dimension reads the radius-kind value (see the circledim records)"
    Err.Clear
    swSketchMgr.InsertSketch True
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sketch.close-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteStep 1, "context", "failed", "the sketch could not be closed"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    ReportContext "closed", verified
    If Not verified Then
        WriteStep 1, "context", "failed", "the closed-sketch context is not verified; the feature call is refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.ClearSelection2 True
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("clearselection-" & tag, n, d, "stage=preselect")
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteStep 1, "selection", "failed", "selections could not be cleared before selecting the profile"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    Set extSel = swDoc.Extension
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("selectsketch-" & tag, n, d, "stage=extension-acquire")
    If n <> 0 Or extSel Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep 3, "extrude", "failed", "the Extension could not be acquired; the profile sketch cannot be selected"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    ok = extSel.SelectByID2(skName, "SKETCH", 0#, 0#, 0#, False, 0, Nothing, swSelectOption_e.swSelectOptionDefault)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("selectsketch-" & tag, n, d, "stage=selectbyname name=" & skName & " result=" & CStr(ok))
    If n <> 0 Or Not ok Then
        WriteStep 3, "extrude", "failed", "the profile sketch " & skName & " could not be selected; the extrusion is not attempted (setup)"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    result = 1
    WriteLine LineFor("featureextrusion2-" & tag, 0, "", "entering: FeatureExtrusion2(True, False, False, swEndCondBlind, swEndCondBlind, 0.012, 0#, False, False, False, False, 0#, 0#, False, False, False, False, True, True, True, 0, 0#, False)")
    Err.Clear
    Set feat = gFeatMgr.FeatureExtrusion2(True, False, False, swEndConditions_e.swEndCondBlind, swEndConditions_e.swEndCondBlind, 0.012, 0#, False, False, False, False, 0#, 0#, False, False, False, False, True, True, True, 0, 0#, False)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("featureextrusion2-" & tag, n, d, "outcome")
    If n <> 0 Or feat Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep 3, "extrude", "failed", "the blind extrusion (Dir=False) was not created; the side cross-check is incomplete"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    featName = feat.Name
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("feature-name-" & tag, n, d, "name=" & featName)
    nameOk = True
    featShown = featName
    If n <> 0 Or Trim(featName) = "" Then
        nameOk = False
        featShown = "(name unavailable)"
        WriteLine LineFor("feature-name-" & tag, -1, "name unavailable", "the D1 lookup cannot be constructed; its key is never issued empty")
    End If
    WriteStep 3, "extrude", "created", "blind 0.012 m, Dir=False, feature " & featShown
    ReportContext "closed", verified
    If Not verified Then
        WriteStep 4, "measure-" & tag, "failed", "the post-feature context is not verified; measurements are refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.ClearSelection2 True
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("clearselection-" & tag, n, d, "stage=premeasure")
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteStep 4, "measure-" & tag, "failed", "selections could not be cleared before the measurements"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    measOk = True
    BoxEvidence tag, ok
    If Not ok Then measOk = False
    If nameOk Then
        DimEvidence "dim-d1-" & tag, "D1@" & featName, True, ok
        If Not ok Then measOk = False
    Else
        WriteLine LineFor("dim-d1-" & tag, -1, "lookup unavailable", "required: no feature name; the D1 identity is missing")
        measOk = False
    End If
    If measOk Then
        WriteStep 4, "measure-" & tag, "created", "circle-kind evidence, map entries and side captured; box form and all 6 components captured; D1 identity captured"
        result = 0
    Else
        WriteStep 4, "measure-" & tag, "failed", "a required observation is missing"
    End If
CaseCleanup:
    On Error Resume Next
    If isFinal And mode = "keep" Then
        ok = OwnedHandoffVerified(tag, handoffTitle)
        If ok Then
            WriteStep 5, "owned-document", "kept-open", handoffTitle
        Else
            WriteStep 5, "owned-document", "failed", "the keep-mode handoff is unverified; the document is not reported as retained"
            result = 3
            CloseOwnedDoc closedOk
            If Not closedOk Then WriteStep 5, "close", "failed", "the unverified handoff could not be confirmed closed"
        End If
    Else
        CloseOwnedDoc closedOk
        If Not closedOk Then
            WriteStep 5, "close", "failed", "the owned document could not be confirmed closed"
            result = 3
        End If
    End If
    Set swDoc = Nothing
    Set swSketchMgr = Nothing
    Set gFeatMgr = Nothing
    RunCylinderCase = result
End Function

' The parameter-change case: the emitter's full box construction (mapped
' drawing, shape contract, both size dimensions), then the length
' dimension driven to 1.5x its drawn value and a full corner readback -
' the shape contract's behavioural evidence. No feature is created.
Function RunEditCase(ByVal tag As String, ByVal isFinal As Boolean, ByVal mode As String) As Long
    Dim result As Long
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim verified As Boolean
    Dim skName As String
    Dim handoffTitle As String
    Dim closedOk As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    Dim ln0 As Object
    Dim ln1 As Object
    Dim ln2 As Object
    Dim ln3 As Object
    Dim dmLen As Object
    Dim dmWid As Object
    Dim axU As Long
    Dim axV As Long
    On Error Resume Next
    result = 2
    WriteLine LineFor("case-" & tag, 0, "", "entering: mapped box with the shape contract, then the length dimension driven to 0.06 (1.5x of 0.04)")
    Err.Clear
    Set swDoc = swApp.NewDocument(gTemplate, 0, 0, 0)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("document.new-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or swDoc Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep -1, "document.new", "failed", "the fresh part for " & tag & " could not be created"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    Set swSketchMgr = swDoc.SketchManager
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sketchmgr-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or swSketchMgr Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep -1, "sketchmgr", "failed", "no sketch manager for " & tag
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Err.Clear
    Set gFeatMgr = swDoc.FeatureManager
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("featuremgr-" & tag, n, d, "")
    If n <> 0 Or gFeatMgr Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep -1, "featuremgr", "failed", "no feature manager for " & tag
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    If Not OpenSketchOnPlaneXY(skName) Then
        WriteStep 0, "sketch.open", "failed", "no plane carries the source-XY geometric frame (translation at the model origin, normal parallel to +Z); probed: " & gProbeLog & "; tree scan saw: " & TreeSummary()
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 0, "sketch.open", "created", gProbeLog & "sketch feature " & skName
    If Not ComputeMap() Then
        WriteStep 0, "map", "failed", "the adaptation map could not be computed fail-closed from the probed frame; the case is refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 0, "map", "created", "m00=" & Trim(Str(gMap00)) & " m01=" & Trim(Str(gMap01)) & " m10=" & Trim(Str(gMap10)) & " m11=" & Trim(Str(gMap11)) & " side=" & Trim(Str(gMapSide)) & " frame " & FrameTextEx()
    ReportContext "active", verified
    If Not verified Then
        WriteStep 1, "context", "failed", "the active-sketch context is not verified"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    Set ln0 = MappedLine(tag, 1, 0.01, 0.02, 0.05, 0.02)
    Set ln1 = MappedLine(tag, 2, 0.05, 0.02, 0.05, 0.035)
    Set ln2 = MappedLine(tag, 3, 0.05, 0.035, 0.01, 0.035)
    Set ln3 = MappedLine(tag, 4, 0.01, 0.035, 0.01, 0.02)
    If ln0 Is Nothing Or ln1 Is Nothing Or ln2 Is Nothing Or ln3 Is Nothing Then
        WriteStep 2, "profile", "failed", "the mapped box profile is incomplete; the edit-follow pin is refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 2, "profile", "created", "four mapped lines at the mapped corners of SC u 0.010..0.050 v 0.020..0.035"
    If Not ShapeContract(tag, ln0, ln1, ln2, ln3, axU, axV) Then
        WriteStep 2, "shape", "failed", "the shape contract did not apply; the edit-follow pin is refused"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    WriteStep 2, "shape", "created", "4 sgCOINCIDENT + classified h/v (u class " & Trim(Str(axU)) & ", v class " & Trim(Str(axV)) & ") + sgFix on the corner"
    If Not SizeDim(tag & "-length", ln0, 0.04, dmLen) Then
        WriteStep 2, "dim-length", "failed", "the length dimension evidence is incomplete"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    If Not SizeDim(tag & "-width", ln1, 0.015, dmWid) Then
        WriteStep 2, "dim-width", "failed", "the width dimension evidence is incomplete"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    ' The parameter change: drive the length dimension to 1.5x its drawn
    ' value and let the solver follow. The emitter's own sequence applies:
    ' EditRebuild3 EXITS sketch edit, so the sketch is re-entered by name
    ' before any further sketch API call.
    result = 1
    Err.Clear
    dmLen.SystemValue = 0.06
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("edit-length-" & tag, n, d, "stage=systemvalue write 0.06 (was 0.04)")
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteStep 3, "edit", "failed", "the length value edit did not stick"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    If Not ReenterSketch(skName) Then
        WriteStep 3, "edit", "failed", "the sketch could not be rebuilt and re-entered after the value edit"
        GoTo CaseCleanup
    End If
    ReportCorners tag, ln0, ln1, ln2, ln3
    WriteStep 3, "edit", "created", "the length value edit was applied and the corner readback is captured (see the corner records)"
    WriteStep 4, "measure-" & tag, "created", "every endpoint coordinate, both edge lengths and the closure are captured"
    result = 0
CaseCleanup:
    On Error Resume Next
    If isFinal And mode = "keep" Then
        ok = OwnedHandoffVerified(tag, handoffTitle)
        If ok Then
            WriteStep 5, "owned-document", "kept-open", handoffTitle
        Else
            WriteStep 5, "owned-document", "failed", "the keep-mode handoff is unverified; the document is not reported as retained"
            result = 3
            CloseOwnedDoc closedOk
            If Not closedOk Then WriteStep 5, "close", "failed", "the unverified handoff could not be confirmed closed"
        End If
    Else
        CloseOwnedDoc closedOk
        If Not closedOk Then
            WriteStep 5, "close", "failed", "the owned document could not be confirmed closed"
            result = 3
        End If
    End If
    Set swDoc = Nothing
    Set swSketchMgr = Nothing
    Set gFeatMgr = Nothing
    RunEditCase = result
End Function

' The emitter's MapU/MapV exactly: s = u*gMap00 + v*gMap10, t =
' u*gMap01 + v*gMap11 (the probe's own map state).
Function MapU(ByVal u As Double, ByVal v As Double) As Double
    MapU = u * gMap00 + v * gMap10
End Function

Function MapV(ByVal u As Double, ByVal v As Double) As Double
    MapV = u * gMap01 + v * gMap11
End Function

' The emitter's AxisClass exactly: where the SC u (or v) direction lands
' in the sketch axes - 0 = s, 1 = t, -1 = not axis-aligned.
Function MapClass(ByVal isU As Boolean) As Long
    Dim c0 As Double
    Dim c1 As Double
    MapClass = -1
    If isU Then
        c0 = gMap00
        c1 = gMap01
    Else
        c0 = gMap10
        c1 = gMap11
    End If
    If Abs(Abs(c0) - 1#) <= 0.000001 And Abs(c1) <= 0.000001 Then MapClass = 0
    If Abs(Abs(c1) - 1#) <= 0.000001 And Abs(c0) <= 0.000001 Then MapClass = 1
End Function

' One mapped profile line: the emitter's CreateLine call shape with the
' map applied to both endpoints. Nothing = the line is missing.
Function MappedLine(ByVal tag As String, ByVal idx As Long, ByVal u1 As Double, ByVal v1 As Double, ByVal u2 As Double, ByVal v2 As Double) As Object
    Dim ln As Object
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    Set MappedLine = Nothing
    Err.Clear
    Set ln = swSketchMgr.CreateLine(MapU(u1, v1), MapV(u1, v1), 0#, MapU(u2, v2), MapV(u2, v2), 0#)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("mapped-line" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, n, d, "stage=createline")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If ln Is Nothing Then
        WriteLine LineFor("mapped-line" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, -1, "returned Nothing", "stage=createline")
        Exit Function
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("mapped-line" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, 0, "", "created type=" & TypeName(ln) & " SC from " & Vec3Text(u1, v1, 0#) & " to " & Vec3Text(u2, v2, 0#))
    Set MappedLine = ln
End Function

' The emitter's circle drawing: mapped centre, radius unchanged.
Function MappedCircle(ByVal tag As String, ByVal u As Double, ByVal v As Double, ByVal r As Double) As Object
    Dim ci As Object
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    Set MappedCircle = Nothing
    Err.Clear
    Set ci = swSketchMgr.CreateCircleByRadius(MapU(u, v), MapV(u, v), 0#, r)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("mapped-circle-" & tag, n, d, "stage=createcirclebyradius")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If ci Is Nothing Then
        WriteLine LineFor("mapped-circle-" & tag, -1, "returned Nothing", "stage=createcirclebyradius")
        Exit Function
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("mapped-circle-" & tag, 0, "", "created type=" & TypeName(ci) & " SC base " & Vec3Text(u, v, 0#) & " r " & Trim(Str(r)))
    Set MappedCircle = ci
End Function

' The emitter's box shape contract: coincident corners closing the
' contour, classified horizontal/vertical relations pinning rectangularity
' and edge directions, and the corner fix anchoring the literal placement.
' SketchAddConstraints has no return value (API doc), so each application
' is established behaviourally - box-edit-follow's corner readback is the
' evidence; at creation a pre-held predicate is indistinguishable (the
' recorded limitation class). False = the contract did not fully apply.
Function ShapeContract(ByVal tag As String, ByVal ln0 As Object, ByVal ln1 As Object, ByVal ln2 As Object, ByVal ln3 As Object, ByRef axU As Long, ByRef axV As Long) As Boolean
    Dim pA As Object
    Dim pB As Object
    Dim nameU As String
    Dim nameV As String
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    ShapeContract = False
    If Not CoincidentPair(tag, 1, ln0, ln1) Then Exit Function
    If Not CoincidentPair(tag, 2, ln1, ln2) Then Exit Function
    If Not CoincidentPair(tag, 3, ln2, ln3) Then Exit Function
    If Not CoincidentPair(tag, 4, ln3, ln0) Then Exit Function
    axU = MapClass(True)
    axV = MapClass(False)
    WriteLine LineFor("shape-class-" & tag, 0, "", "u class " & Trim(Str(axU)) & " v class " & Trim(Str(axV)))
    If axU < 0 Or axV < 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("shape-class-" & tag, -1, "not axis-aligned", "the classified relation kinds cannot be chosen on this map")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If axU = 0 Then nameU = "sgHORIZONTAL2D" Else nameU = "sgVERTICAL2D"
    If axV = 0 Then nameV = "sgHORIZONTAL2D" Else nameV = "sgVERTICAL2D"
    If Not LevelLine(tag, 1, ln0, nameU) Then Exit Function
    If Not LevelLine(tag, 3, ln2, nameU) Then Exit Function
    If Not LevelLine(tag, 2, ln1, nameV) Then Exit Function
    If Not LevelLine(tag, 4, ln3, nameV) Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set pA = ln0.GetStartPoint2
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("corner-fix-" & tag, n, d, "stage=corner-handle")
    If n <> 0 Or pA Is Nothing Then
        WriteLine LineFor("corner-fix-" & tag, -1, "returned Nothing", "stage=corner-handle")
        Exit Function
    End If
    Err.Clear
    ok = pA.Select(False)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("corner-fix-" & tag, n, d, "stage=select result=" & CStr(ok))
    If n <> 0 Or Not ok Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.SketchAddConstraints "sgFix"
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("corner-fix-" & tag, n, d, "stage=sgFix (no return value)")
    swDoc.ClearSelection2 True
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    ShapeContract = True
End Function

' One coincident corner: the end of one line with the start of the next.
Function CoincidentPair(ByVal tag As String, ByVal idx As Long, ByVal lnA As Object, ByVal lnB As Object) As Boolean
    Dim pA As Object
    Dim pB As Object
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    CoincidentPair = False
    Err.Clear
    Set pA = lnA.GetEndPoint2
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("corner" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, n, d, "stage=end-handle")
    If n <> 0 Or pA Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set pB = lnB.GetStartPoint2
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("corner" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, n, d, "stage=start-handle")
    If n <> 0 Or pB Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    ok = pA.Select(False)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("corner" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, n, d, "stage=select-first result=" & CStr(ok))
    If n <> 0 Or Not ok Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    ok = pB.Select(True)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("corner" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, n, d, "stage=select-second result=" & CStr(ok))
    If n <> 0 Or Not ok Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.SketchAddConstraints "sgCOINCIDENT"
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("corner" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, n, d, "stage=sgCOINCIDENT (no return value)")
    swDoc.ClearSelection2 True
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    CoincidentPair = True
End Function

' One classified level relation on a line (the emitter's classified form).
Function LevelLine(ByVal tag As String, ByVal idx As Long, ByVal ln As Object, ByVal relName As String) As Boolean
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    LevelLine = False
    Err.Clear
    ok = ln.Select(False)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("level" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, n, d, "stage=select result=" & CStr(ok))
    If n <> 0 Or Not ok Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.SketchAddConstraints relName
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("level" & Trim(Str(idx)) & "-" & tag, n, d, "stage=" & relName & " (no return value)")
    swDoc.ClearSelection2 True
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    LevelLine = True
End Function

' One emitter-pattern size dimension on a line: created with the disabled
' input-value toggle, its Name and SystemValue reported WITH THE SIGN, the
' sign resolved as the emitter resolves it, the value written, and the
' behavioural check run (the value edit must carry the measured length).
Function SizeDim(ByVal tag As String, ByVal ln As Object, ByVal expect As Double, ByRef dmOut As Object) As Boolean
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim dd As Object
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    Dim v As Variant
    Dim created As Double
    Dim signVal As Double
    Dim chk As Double
    Dim v1 As Variant
    Dim v2 As Variant
    On Error Resume Next
    SizeDim = False
    Set dmOut = Nothing
    Err.Clear
    ok = ln.Select(False)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=select result=" & CStr(ok))
    If n <> 0 Or Not ok Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set dd = swDoc.AddDimension2(0#, 0#, 0#)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=adddimension2")
    If n <> 0 Or dd Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set dmOut = dd.GetDimension2(0)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=getdimension2")
    If n <> 0 Or dmOut Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    v = dmOut.Name
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=name -> " & CStr(v))
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    v = dmOut.SystemValue
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=systemvalue")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not NumDecode("sizedim-" & tag, "systemvalue", v, created) Then Exit Function
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, 0, "", "created value=" & Trim(Str(created)) & " (SI, sign carried) against source " & Trim(Str(expect)))
    If Abs(created - expect) <= 0.000001 Then
        signVal = 1#
    ElseIf Abs(created + expect) <= 0.000001 Then
        signVal = -1#
    Else
        WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, -1, "value mismatch", "created " & Trim(Str(created)) & " matches neither sign of " & Trim(Str(expect)))
        Exit Function
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, 0, "", "signVal=" & Trim(Str(signVal)))
    Err.Clear
    dmOut.SystemValue = signVal * expect
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=systemvalue write " & Trim(Str(signVal * expect)))
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    v1 = ln.GetStartPoint
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=behaviour start")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    v2 = ln.GetEndPoint
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=behaviour end")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If Not BehaviourLength("sizedim-" & tag, v1, v2, chk) Then Exit Function
    If Abs(chk - expect) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, -1, "geometry did not follow", "length " & Trim(Str(chk)) & " after driving " & Trim(Str(expect)))
        Exit Function
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("sizedim-" & tag, 0, "", "behaviour check passed: length " & Trim(Str(chk)))
    SizeDim = True
End Function

' The emitter-pattern circle dimension with the kind evidence: the created
' value is reported against GetRadius AND twice it (the radius-kind vs
' diameter-kind pin), then the emitter's kind guards run verbatim in
' effect - ambiguity and the diameter-kind reading refuse exactly as the
' emitter refuses them - and only a clean radius-kind reading writes the
' value and reports kindOk = True.
Function CircleDim(ByVal tag As String, ByVal ci As Object, ByVal r As Double, ByRef dmOut As Object, ByRef kindOk As Boolean) As Boolean
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim dd As Object
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    Dim v As Variant
    Dim created As Double
    Dim rad As Double
    Dim signVal As Double
    On Error Resume Next
    CircleDim = False
    kindOk = False
    Set dmOut = Nothing
    Err.Clear
    ok = ci.Select(False)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=select result=" & CStr(ok))
    If n <> 0 Or Not ok Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set dd = swDoc.AddDimension2(0#, 0#, 0#)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=adddimension2")
    If n <> 0 Or dd Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set dmOut = dd.GetDimension2(0)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=getdimension2")
    If n <> 0 Or dmOut Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    v = dmOut.Name
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=name -> " & CStr(v))
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    v = dmOut.SystemValue
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=systemvalue")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not NumDecode("circledim-" & tag, "systemvalue", v, created) Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    v = ci.GetRadius
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=getradius")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not NumDecode("circledim-" & tag, "getradius", v, rad) Then Exit Function
    WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, 0, "", "kind evidence: created=" & Trim(Str(created)) & " getradius=" & Trim(Str(rad)) & " twice-getradius=" & Trim(Str(2# * rad)))
    If Abs(Abs(created) - r) <= 0.000001 And Abs(Abs(created) - 2# * r) <= 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, -1, "kind ambiguous", "the radius- and diameter-kind readings coincide within tolerance at this scale (source r " & Trim(Str(r)) & ")")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs(Abs(created) - 2# * r) <= 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, -1, "diameter-kind reading", "the created value matches twice the radius; the emitter refuses this reading")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs(Abs(created) - r) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, -1, "value mismatch", "created " & Trim(Str(created)) & " matches neither radius nor diameter reading of " & Trim(Str(r)))
        Exit Function
    End If
    kindOk = True
    If Abs(created - r) <= 0.000001 Then
        signVal = 1#
    Else
        signVal = -1#
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, 0, "", "radius-kind reading confirmed; signVal=" & Trim(Str(signVal)))
    Err.Clear
    dmOut.SystemValue = signVal * r
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=systemvalue write " & Trim(Str(signVal * r)))
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    v = ci.GetRadius
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, n, d, "stage=behaviour getradius")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("circledim-" & tag, "behaviour getradius", v, rad) Then Exit Function
    If Abs(rad - r) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, -1, "geometry did not follow", "radius " & Trim(Str(rad)) & " after driving " & Trim(Str(r)))
        Exit Function
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("circledim-" & tag, 0, "", "behaviour check passed: radius " & Trim(Str(rad)))
    CircleDim = True
End Function

' The full corner readback after the parameter change: every endpoint of
' the four lines, both edge lengths and the closure distances - the shape
' contract's behavioural evidence. The numbers are reported, never
' interpreted here.
Sub ReportCorners(ByVal tag As String, ByVal ln0 As Object, ByVal ln1 As Object, ByVal ln2 As Object, ByVal ln3 As Object)
    Dim x1 As Double
    Dim y1 As Double
    Dim z1 As Double
    Dim x2 As Double
    Dim y2 As Double
    Dim z2 As Double
    Dim x3 As Double
    Dim y3 As Double
    Dim z3 As Double
    Dim x4 As Double
    Dim y4 As Double
    Dim z4 As Double
    Dim chk As Double
    On Error Resume Next
    If Not LineCorners("corner-readback-" & tag & "-ln0", ln0, x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2) Then Exit Sub
    If Not LineCorners("corner-readback-" & tag & "-ln1", ln1, x3, y3, z3, x4, y4, z4) Then Exit Sub
    chk = Sqr((x4 - x3) * (x4 - x3) + (y4 - y3) * (y4 - y3))
    WriteLine LineFor("corner-readback-" & tag, 0, "", "ln1 length=" & Trim(Str(chk)))
    If Not LineCorners("corner-readback-" & tag & "-ln2", ln2, x3, y3, z3, x4, y4, z4) Then Exit Sub
    If Not LineCorners("corner-readback-" & tag & "-ln3", ln3, x3, y3, z3, x4, y4, z4) Then Exit Sub
    chk = Sqr((x4 - x1) * (x4 - x1) + (y4 - y1) * (y4 - y1))
    WriteLine LineFor("corner-readback-" & tag, 0, "", "closure ln3-end to ln0-start distance=" & Trim(Str(chk)))
    chk = Sqr((x2 - x1) * (x2 - x1) + (y2 - y1) * (y2 - y1))
    WriteLine LineFor("corner-readback-" & tag, 0, "", "ln0 length=" & Trim(Str(chk)))
End Sub

' One line's endpoint pair as report records; False = a required readback
' is missing.
Function LineCorners(ByVal tag As String, ByVal ln As Object, ByRef x1 As Double, ByRef y1 As Double, ByRef z1 As Double, ByRef x2 As Double, ByRef y2 As Double, ByRef z2 As Double) As Boolean
    Dim v As Variant
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    LineCorners = False
    Err.Clear
    v = ln.GetStartPoint
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=getstartpoint")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If Not ReadVec(tag, "start", v, x1, y1, z1) Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    v = ln.GetEndPoint
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=getendpoint")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If Not ReadVec(tag, "end", v, x2, y2, z2) Then Exit Function
    WriteLine LineFor(tag, 0, "", "start " & Vec3Text(x1, y1, z1) & " end " & Vec3Text(x2, y2, z2))
    LineCorners = True
End Function

' The three components of one returned vector, each extracted at its own
' captured stage and decoded through NumDecode; a failed extraction is
' recorded and can never pass.
Function ReadVec(ByVal tag As String, ByVal stage As String, ByVal v As Variant, ByRef x As Double, ByRef y As Double, ByRef z As Double) As Boolean
    Dim one As Variant
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    ReadVec = False
    Err.Clear
    one = v(0)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=" & stage & "-x extraction")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not NumDecode(tag, stage & "-x", one, x) Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    one = v(1)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=" & stage & "-y extraction")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not NumDecode(tag, stage & "-y", one, y) Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    one = v(2)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=" & stage & "-z extraction")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not NumDecode(tag, stage & "-z", one, z) Then Exit Function
    ReadVec = True
End Function

' The emitter's behavioural length check over a line's endpoint pair.
Function BehaviourLength(ByVal tag As String, ByVal v1 As Variant, ByVal v2 As Variant, ByRef chk As Double) As Boolean
    Dim x1 As Double
    Dim y1 As Double
    Dim z1 As Double
    Dim x2 As Double
    Dim y2 As Double
    Dim z2 As Double
    On Error Resume Next
    BehaviourLength = False
    chk = 0#
    If Not ReadVec(tag, "behaviour-start", v1, x1, y1, z1) Then Exit Function
    If Not ReadVec(tag, "behaviour-end", v2, x2, y2, z2) Then Exit Function
    chk = Sqr((x2 - x1) * (x2 - x1) + (y2 - y1) * (y2 - y1))
    BehaviourLength = True
End Function

' The emitter's SolveSketch equivalent: EditRebuild3 EXITS sketch edit
' (seat-measured), so the sketch is rebuilt and re-entered by name, and
' the final state is verified.
Function ReenterSketch(ByVal nm As String) As Boolean
    Dim sk As Object
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    ReenterSketch = False
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.EditRebuild3
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("reenter-sketch", n, d, "stage=editrebuild3 (exits sketch edit)")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set sk = swSketchMgr.ActiveSketch
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("reenter-sketch", n, d, "stage=activesketch")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If sk Is Nothing Then
        Err.Clear
        swDoc.Extension.SelectByID2 nm, "SKETCH", 0#, 0#, 0#, False, 0, Nothing, swSelectOption_e.swSelectOptionDefault
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("reenter-sketch", n, d, "stage=selectbyname " & nm)
        If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
        Err.Clear
        swSketchMgr.InsertSketch True
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("reenter-sketch", n, d, "stage=insertsketch")
        If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
        Err.Clear
        Set sk = swSketchMgr.ActiveSketch
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("reenter-sketch", n, d, "stage=activesketch-reget")
        If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    End If
    If sk Is Nothing Then
        WriteLine LineFor("reenter-sketch", -1, "not re-entered", "sketch " & nm & " could not be re-entered")
        Exit Function
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("reenter-sketch", 0, "", "verified: sketch " & nm & " is active again")
    ReenterSketch = True
End Function

' The adaptation map from the probed frame, fail-closed exactly like the
' emitter's PublishMap: the 16-entry transform form, finite decoded
' entries, scale 1, unit axes, mutual orthogonality, the right-handed 3D
' frame and the normal parallel to the source +Z. For the source-XY plane
' the map entries are m00 = a(0), m01 = a(1), m10 = a(3), m11 = a(4) and
' the side is sign(a(8)) (source u = +X, v = +Y, n = +Z). Nothing is
' stored before the complete validation passes.
Function ComputeMap() As Boolean
    Dim skObj As Object
    Dim tr As Object
    Dim a As Variant
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    Dim lb As Long
    Dim ub As Long
    Dim ux As Double
    Dim uy As Double
    Dim uz As Double
    Dim vx As Double
    Dim vy As Double
    Dim vz As Double
    Dim nx As Double
    Dim ny As Double
    Dim nz As Double
    Dim sc As Double
    Dim x9 As Double
    Dim x10 As Double
    Dim x11 As Double
    Dim m00 As Double
    Dim m01 As Double
    Dim m10 As Double
    Dim m11 As Double
    Dim side As Long
    On Error Resume Next
    ComputeMap = False
    Err.Clear
    Set skObj = swSketchMgr.ActiveSketch
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("map", n, d, "stage=activesketch")
    If n <> 0 Or skObj Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set tr = skObj.ModelToSketchTransform
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("map", n, d, "stage=transform")
    If n <> 0 Or tr Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    a = tr.ArrayData
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("map", n, d, "stage=arraydata")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    lb = LBound(a)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("map", n, d, "stage=lbound")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    ub = UBound(a)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("map", n, d, "stage=ubound")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If lb <> 0 Or ub <> 15 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "unexpected form", "lbound=" & Trim(Str(lb)) & " ubound=" & Trim(Str(ub)) & " (expected zero-based 0..15)")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not NumDecode("map", "scale", a(12), sc) Then Exit Function
    If Abs(sc - 1#) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "scale not 1", "scale " & Trim(Str(sc)))
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not NumDecode("map", "translation-x", a(9), x9) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "translation-y", a(10), x10) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "translation-z", a(11), x11) Then Exit Function
    If Abs(x9) > 0.000001 Or Abs(x10) > 0.000001 Or Abs(x11) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "translation not at origin", Vec3Text(x9, x10, x11))
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not NumDecode("map", "axis-ux", a(0), ux) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "axis-uy", a(3), uy) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "axis-uz", a(6), uz) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "axis-vx", a(1), vx) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "axis-vy", a(4), vy) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "axis-vz", a(7), vz) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "axis-nx", a(2), nx) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "axis-ny", a(5), ny) Then Exit Function
    If Not NumDecode("map", "axis-nz", a(8), nz) Then Exit Function
    If Abs(Sqr(ux * ux + uy * uy + uz * uz) - 1#) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "u not unit", Vec3Text(ux, uy, uz))
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs(Sqr(vx * vx + vy * vy + vz * vz) - 1#) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "v not unit", Vec3Text(vx, vy, vz))
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs(Sqr(nx * nx + ny * ny + nz * nz) - 1#) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "n not unit", Vec3Text(nx, ny, nz))
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs(ux * vx + uy * vy + uz * vz) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "u and v not orthogonal", "")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs(ux * nx + uy * ny + uz * nz) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "u and n not orthogonal", "")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs(vx * nx + vy * ny + vz * nz) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "v and n not orthogonal", "")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs((uy * vz - uz * vy) - nx) > 0.000001 Or Abs((uz * vx - ux * vz) - ny) > 0.000001 Or Abs((ux * vy - uy * vx) - nz) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "frame not right-handed", "u x v does not equal n")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs(Abs(nz) - 1#) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("map", -1, "normal not parallel to +Z", Vec3Text(nx, ny, nz))
        Exit Function
    End If
    m00 = ux
    m01 = vx
    m10 = uy
    m11 = vy
    side = 1
    If nz < 0 Then side = -1
    gMap00 = m00
    gMap01 = m01
    gMap10 = m10
    gMap11 = m11
    gMapSide = side
    WriteLine LineFor("map", 0, "", "published m00=" & Trim(Str(m00)) & " m01=" & Trim(Str(m01)) & " m10=" & Trim(Str(m10)) & " m11=" & Trim(Str(m11)) & " side=" & Trim(Str(side)))
    ComputeMap = True
End Function

' The emitter's PlaneIsSource("XY") acceptance exactly: the probe sketch
' must sit on the geometric source plane - translation at the model
' origin and the normal parallel to +Z (either sign). Strict frame
' equality is NOT required (the map adapts); every probed frame is
' reported by the caller through FrameTextEx.
Function PlaneIsSourceXY() As Boolean
    Dim skObj As Object
    Dim tr As Object
    Dim a As Variant
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    PlaneIsSourceXY = False
    Err.Clear
    Set skObj = swSketchMgr.ActiveSketch
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("plane-accept", n, d, "stage=activesketch")
    If n <> 0 Or skObj Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set tr = skObj.ModelToSketchTransform
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("plane-accept", n, d, "stage=transform")
    If n <> 0 Or tr Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    a = tr.ArrayData
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("plane-accept", n, d, "stage=arraydata")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If Abs(a(9)) > 0.000001 Or Abs(a(10)) > 0.000001 Or Abs(a(11)) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("plane-accept", -1, "translation not at origin", Vec3Text(a(9), a(10), a(11)))
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Abs(Abs(a(8)) - 1#) > 0.000001 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("plane-accept", -1, "normal not parallel to +Z", Vec3Text(a(2), a(5), a(8)))
        Exit Function
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("plane-accept", 0, "", "accepted source-XY geometric plane: " & FrameTextEx())
    PlaneIsSourceXY = True
End Function

' Open a sketch on the first plane-like feature whose probe sketch sits on
' the source-XY geometric plane (the emitter's acceptance); fail-closed on
' every uncertain state. The sketch's feature identity is acquired at its
' own captured, Nothing-checked stage (the documented Sketch->Feature
' assignment; ISketch exposes no GetFeature) and its name is returned for
' the later explicit selection. Every call emits its own named capture
' record and every failure is recorded in gProbeLog with its captured
' error. A rejected plane's probe sketch is deleted by the verified
' DiscardProbeSketch algorithm; if that deletion cannot be confirmed, the
' run is failed.
Function OpenSketchOnPlaneXY(ByRef skNameOut As String) As Boolean
    Dim feat As Object
    Dim skObj As Object
    Dim skFeat As SldWorks.Feature
    Dim nm As String
    Dim fn As String
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    OpenSketchOnPlaneXY = False
    skNameOut = ""
    gProbeLog = ""
    Err.Clear
    Set feat = swDoc.FirstFeature
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("plane-probe", n, d, "stage=firstfeature")
    If n <> 0 Then
        gProbeLog = gProbeLog & "stage=firstfeature err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
        Exit Function
    End If
    Do While Not feat Is Nothing
        Err.Clear
        nm = feat.GetTypeName2()
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("plane-probe", n, d, "stage=typename")
        If n <> 0 Then
            gProbeLog = gProbeLog & "stage=typename err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
            Exit Function
        End If
        If InStr(1, nm, "lane", vbTextCompare) > 0 Then
            Err.Clear
            fn = feat.Name
            n = Err.Number
            d = Err.Description
            WriteLine LineFor("plane-probe", n, d, "stage=name")
            If n <> 0 Then
                gProbeLog = gProbeLog & "stage=name err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
                Exit Function
            End If
            Err.Clear
            ok = feat.Select(False)
            n = Err.Number
            d = Err.Description
            WriteLine LineFor("plane-probe", n, d, "stage=select plane=" & fn & " result=" & CStr(ok))
            If n <> 0 Then
                gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": select err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
            ElseIf Not ok Then
                gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": select returned false; "
            Else
                Err.Clear
                swSketchMgr.InsertSketch True
                n = Err.Number
                d = Err.Description
                WriteLine LineFor("plane-probe", n, d, "stage=insertsketch plane=" & fn)
                If n <> 0 Then
                    gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": insertsketch err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
                    Exit Function
                End If
                Err.Clear
                Set skObj = swSketchMgr.ActiveSketch
                n = Err.Number
                d = Err.Description
                WriteLine LineFor("plane-probe", n, d, "stage=activesketch plane=" & fn)
                If n <> 0 Then
                    gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": activesketch err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
                    Exit Function
                End If
                If skObj Is Nothing Then
                    gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": opened but no active sketch object; "
                Else
                    Err.Clear
                    Set skFeat = skObj
                    n = Err.Number
                    d = Err.Description
                    WriteLine LineFor("plane-probe", n, d, "stage=sketch-feature-acquire plane=" & fn)
                    If n <> 0 Then
                        gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": sketch-feature acquire err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
                        Exit Function
                    End If
                    If skFeat Is Nothing Then
                        gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": sketch-feature acquire returned Nothing; "
                        Exit Function
                    End If
                    If PlaneIsSourceXY() Then
                        Err.Clear
                        skNameOut = skFeat.Name
                        n = Err.Number
                        d = Err.Description
                        WriteLine LineFor("plane-probe", n, d, "stage=sketch-feature-name plane=" & fn & " name=" & skNameOut)
                        If n <> 0 Or Trim(skNameOut) = "" Then
                            gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": sketch-feature name err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
                            Exit Function
                        End If
                        gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": opened; frame " & FrameTextEx() & "; "
                        OpenSketchOnPlaneXY = True
                        Exit Function
                    Else
                        gProbeLog = gProbeLog & fn & ": " & FrameTextEx() & "; "
                        If Not DiscardProbeSketch(skFeat) Then
                            gProbeLog = gProbeLog & "PROBE SKETCH NOT CONFIRMED DELETED; "
                            Exit Function
                        End If
                    End If
                End If
            End If
        End If
        Err.Clear
        Set feat = feat.GetNextFeature
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("plane-probe", n, d, "stage=nextfeature")
        If n <> 0 Then
            gProbeLog = gProbeLog & "stage=nextfeature err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
            Exit Function
        End If
    Loop
End Function

' The body's bounding box: the exact returned form (zero-based
' one-dimensional, 6 components - rank probed, not assumed) and every
' component extracted with its own captured error BEFORE decoding (a
' failed extraction is recorded and can never pass), then decoded
' through NumDecode. Required evidence: the call must succeed and all
' six components must decode; a different form is reported verbatim and
' refused - components are never interpreted against a wrong form and
' never substituted with defaults.
Sub BoxEvidence(ByVal tag As String, ByRef ok As Boolean)
    Dim pb As SldWorks.PartDoc
    Dim v As Variant
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    Dim tmp As String
    Dim lb As Long
    Dim ub As Long
    Dim i As Long
    Dim vOne As Variant
    Dim comps As String
    Dim bad As Boolean
    Dim x As Double
    On Error Resume Next
    ok = False
    bad = False
    WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, 0, "", "entering: IPartDoc.GetPartBox(True) keeps system units (SI metres)")
    Err.Clear
    Set pb = swDoc
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, n, d, "stage=partdoc-acquire")
    If n <> 0 Or pb Is Nothing Then Exit Sub
    Err.Clear
    v = pb.GetPartBox(True)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, n, d, "stage=call outcome")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, 0, "", "stage=call outcome: a value came back")
    Err.Clear
    tmp = TypeName(v)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, n, d, "stage=form typename")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    Err.Clear
    lb = LBound(v)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, n, d, "stage=form lbound (type=" & tmp & ")")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    Err.Clear
    ub = UBound(v)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, n, d, "stage=form ubound (type=" & tmp & ")")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, 0, "", "stage=form type=" & tmp & " lbound=" & Trim(Str(lb)) & " ubound=" & Trim(Str(ub)))
    If lb <> 0 Or ub <> 5 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, -1, "unexpected form", "stage=form check: zero-based 6 components (0..5) expected; the values are not interpreted")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    Err.Clear
    ub = UBound(v, 2)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n = 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, -1, "a second dimension exists", "stage=rank-probe")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, n, d, "stage=rank-probe (error 9 = one-dimensional, expected)")
    If n <> 9 Then Exit Sub
    comps = ""
    For i = 0 To 5
        Err.Clear
        vOne = Empty
        vOne = v(i)
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        If n <> 0 Then
            WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, n, d, "stage=component" & Trim(Str(i)) & " extraction")
            bad = True
        ElseIf NumDecode("getpartbox-" & tag, "component" & Trim(Str(i)), vOne, x) Then
            tmp = Trim(Str(x))
            comps = comps & " c" & Trim(Str(i)) & "=" & tmp
        Else
            bad = True
        End If
    Next i
    If bad Then Exit Sub
    WriteLine LineFor("getpartbox-" & tag, 0, "", "box components:" & comps & " (documented form: c0..c2 one diagonal corner, c3..c5 the other; approximate)")
    ok = True
End Sub

' One dimension identity: the lookup key, the returned Name and the
' SystemValue in SI base units (lengths in metres, angles in radians),
' each at its own captured stage. Required evidence: a nonblank returned
' Name and a decoded numeric SystemValue - neither is ever substituted
' with a default. required = True makes a missing identity a measurement
' failure; required = False is an informative look (absence is not fatal)
' and is labeled so in every record.
Sub DimEvidence(ByVal tag As String, ByVal key As String, ByVal required As Boolean, ByRef ok As Boolean)
    Dim dm As Object
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    Dim tmp As String
    Dim v As Variant
    Dim sv As Double
    On Error Resume Next
    ok = False
    WriteLine LineFor(tag, 0, "", "entering: Parameter(" & key & ") required=" & CStr(required))
    Err.Clear
    Set dm = swDoc.Parameter(key)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=lookup " & key & " required=" & CStr(required))
        Exit Sub
    End If
    If dm Is Nothing Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, -1, "returned Nothing", "stage=lookup " & key & " required=" & CStr(required))
        Exit Sub
    End If
    Err.Clear
    v = dm.Name
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=name " & key)
        Exit Sub
    End If
    Err.Clear
    tmp = CStr(v)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=name-convert " & key)
        Exit Sub
    End If
    If Trim(tmp) = "" Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, -1, "blank name", "stage=name " & key & " returned a blank identity")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor(tag, 0, "", "stage=name " & key & " -> " & tmp)
    Err.Clear
    v = dm.SystemValue
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=systemvalue " & key)
        Exit Sub
    End If
    If Not NumDecode(tag, "systemvalue " & key, v, sv) Then Exit Sub
    WriteLine LineFor(tag, 0, "", "stage=systemvalue " & key & " = " & Trim(Str(sv)) & " (SI)")
    ok = True
End Sub

' One numeric component: Empty/Null/nonnumeric values are rejected
' BEFORE any coercion (CDbl(Empty) would silently become zero), and the
' conversion is captured at its own named stage. True = x holds the
' decoded value; nothing is ever substituted with a default.
Function NumDecode(ByVal tag As String, ByVal stage As String, ByVal v As Variant, ByRef x As Double) As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    NumDecode = False
    x = 0#
    If IsEmpty(v) Or IsNull(v) Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, -1, "Empty/Null value", "stage=" & stage & " decode refused")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not IsNumeric(v) Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, -1, "nonnumeric value", "stage=" & stage & " decode refused (type=" & TypeName(v) & ")")
        Exit Function
    End If
    Err.Clear
    x = CDbl(v)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor(tag, n, d, "stage=" & stage & " decode")
        Exit Function
    End If
    WriteLine LineFor(tag, 0, "", "stage=" & stage & " value=" & Trim(Str(x)))
    NumDecode = True
End Function

Function LineFor(ByVal which As String, ByVal n As Long, ByVal d As String, ByVal detail As String) As String
    LineFor = "{""type"":""probe"",""member"":""" & JsonStr(which) & """,""err"":" & Trim(Str(n)) & ",""errdesc"":""" & JsonStr(d) & """,""detail"":""" & JsonStr(detail) & """}"
End Function

' Direction equality with sign, on normalized vectors.
Function VecIs(ByVal ax As Double, ByVal ay As Double, ByVal az As Double, ByVal bx As Double, ByVal by As Double, ByVal bz As Double) As Boolean
    Dim L As Double
    L = Sqr(ax * ax + ay * ay + az * az)
    If Abs(L) < 0.000001 Then Exit Function
    VecIs = Abs(ax / L - bx) < 0.000001 And Abs(ay / L - by) < 0.000001 And Abs(az / L - bz) < 0.000001
End Function

' The active sketch's frame as report text. The active-sketch
' acquisition and the transform acquisition are separate captured
' stages; every decode is captured too.
Function FrameTextEx() As String
    Dim skObj As Object
    Dim tr As Object
    Dim a As Variant
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    Err.Clear
    Set skObj = swSketchMgr.ActiveSketch
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        FrameTextEx = "(frame unavailable: activesketch err " & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & ")"
        Exit Function
    End If
    If skObj Is Nothing Then
        FrameTextEx = "(frame unavailable: activesketch returned Nothing)"
        Exit Function
    End If
    Err.Clear
    Set tr = skObj.ModelToSketchTransform
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        FrameTextEx = "(frame unavailable: transform err " & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & ")"
        Exit Function
    End If
    If tr Is Nothing Then
        FrameTextEx = "(frame unavailable: transform returned Nothing)"
        Exit Function
    End If
    Err.Clear
    a = tr.ArrayData
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        FrameTextEx = "(frame unavailable: arraydata err " & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & ")"
        Exit Function
    End If
    Err.Clear
    FrameTextEx = "u=(" & Vec3Text(a(0), a(3), a(6)) & ") v=(" & Vec3Text(a(1), a(4), a(7)) & ") n=(" & Vec3Text(a(2), a(5), a(8)) & ") o=(" & Vec3Text(a(9), a(10), a(11)) & ")"
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then FrameTextEx = "(frame unavailable: index err " & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & ")"
End Function

' Verify the named context against the live sketch state; False = the
' context is NOT verified and no named measurement may proceed.
Sub ReportContext(ByVal ctx As String, ByRef verified As Boolean)
    Dim sk As Object
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    verified = False
    Err.Clear
    Set sk = swSketchMgr.ActiveSketch
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then
        WriteLine LineFor("context-" & ctx, n, d, "active-sketch query failed; context NOT verified")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    If ctx = "active" Then
        If sk Is Nothing Then
            WriteLine LineFor("context-active", -1, "no active sketch", "context NOT verified")
        Else
            verified = True
            WriteLine LineFor("context-active", 0, "", "verified: a sketch is active")
        End If
    Else
        If sk Is Nothing Then
            verified = True
            WriteLine LineFor("context-closed", 0, "", "verified: no sketch is active")
        Else
            WriteLine LineFor("context-closed", -1, "a sketch is still active", "context NOT verified")
        End If
    End If
End Sub

Function Vec3Text(ByVal x As Double, ByVal y As Double, ByVal z As Double) As String
    Vec3Text = Trim(Str(x)) & "," & Trim(Str(y)) & "," & Trim(Str(z))
End Function

' A live feature-tree lookup by name. Returns the feature when a complete
' walk found it; returns Nothing with uncertain = False only when a
' complete walk proves it absent; uncertain = True whenever the walk or
' the name failed. Absence is never inferred from a failed query, and an
' empty name is never sent to any API. Every call is captured at its own
' named stage and recorded.
Function FindFeatureByName(ByVal nm As String, ByRef uncertain As Boolean) As SldWorks.Feature
    Dim feat As SldWorks.Feature
    Dim fn As String
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    Set FindFeatureByName = Nothing
    uncertain = True
    If nm = "" Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set feat = swDoc.FirstFeature
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("find-feature", n, d, "stage=firstfeature")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Do While Not feat Is Nothing
        Err.Clear
        fn = feat.Name
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("find-feature", n, d, "stage=name")
        If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
        If fn = nm Then
            Set FindFeatureByName = feat
            uncertain = False
            WriteLine LineFor("find-feature", 0, "", "found " & nm)
            Exit Function
        End If
        Err.Clear
        Set feat = feat.GetNextFeature
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("find-feature", n, d, "stage=nextfeature")
        If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Loop
    uncertain = False
    WriteLine LineFor("find-feature", 0, "", "complete walk: " & nm & " is absent")
End Function

' Close the probe sketch and delete exactly the feature that was created
' for it - never a blind EditDelete, never a stale-object test. The name
' is captured while the object is alive and validated; the close is
' confirmed; the delete runs only from a captured, error-checked
' selection of the one feature the live tree returns (a raised selection
' never falls through to EditDelete); and the deletion is verified the
' same way. Closing an empty sketch may already have removed it - that
' is a clean result. True = the probe sketch is proven gone; every
' uncertain state fails closed. Every call is captured at its own named
' stage and recorded.
Function DiscardProbeSketch(ByVal skFeat As SldWorks.Feature) As Boolean
    Dim nm As String
    Dim cur As Object
    Dim live As SldWorks.Feature
    Dim uncertain As Boolean
    Dim selOk As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    DiscardProbeSketch = False
    Err.Clear
    nm = skFeat.Name
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("discard-probe-sketch", n, d, "stage=name")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If nm = "" Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Set cur = swSketchMgr.ActiveSketch
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("discard-probe-sketch", n, d, "stage=activesketch")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If Not cur Is Nothing Then
        Err.Clear
        swSketchMgr.InsertSketch True
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("discard-probe-sketch", n, d, "stage=insertsketch-close")
        If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
        Err.Clear
        Set cur = swSketchMgr.ActiveSketch
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("discard-probe-sketch", n, d, "stage=activesketch-reget")
        If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
        If Not cur Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    End If
    Set live = FindFeatureByName(nm, uncertain)
    If live Is Nothing Then
        DiscardProbeSketch = Not uncertain
        WriteLine LineFor("discard-probe-sketch", 0, "", "stage=find outcome: absent=" & CStr(Not uncertain))
        Exit Function
    End If
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.ClearSelection2 True
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("discard-probe-sketch", n, d, "stage=clearselection")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    selOk = live.Select(False)
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("discard-probe-sketch", n, d, "stage=select result=" & CStr(selOk))
    If n <> 0 Or Not selOk Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    swDoc.EditDelete
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("discard-probe-sketch", n, d, "stage=editdelete")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Set live = FindFeatureByName(nm, uncertain)
    DiscardProbeSketch = (live Is Nothing) And (Not uncertain)
    WriteLine LineFor("discard-probe-sketch", 0, "", "stage=verify deleted=" & CStr(DiscardProbeSketch))
End Function

' Live enumeration of the open documents answering to the title: how
' many match, and is the single match the object this macro owns? Every
' call is captured at its own named stage and recorded. False = a query
' failed, which proves nothing and leaves every caller's outcome
' unverified.
Function DocEnumeration(ByVal t As String, ByRef cnt As Long, ByRef isOurs As Boolean) As Boolean
    Dim dd As Object
    Dim t2 As String
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    DocEnumeration = False
    cnt = 0
    isOurs = False
    Err.Clear
    Set dd = swApp.GetFirstDocument
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("doc-enum", n, d, "stage=getfirstdocument")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Do While Not dd Is Nothing
        Err.Clear
        t2 = dd.GetTitle
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("doc-enum", n, d, "stage=gettitle t=" & t2)
        If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
        If t2 = t Then
            cnt = cnt + 1
            If dd Is swDoc Then isOurs = True
        End If
        Err.Clear
        Set dd = dd.GetNext
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        WriteLine LineFor("doc-enum", n, d, "stage=getnext")
        If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Loop
    WriteLine LineFor("doc-enum", 0, "", "complete: matches=" & Trim(Str(cnt)) & " ours=" & CStr(isOurs))
    DocEnumeration = True
End Function

' Close exactly the document this macro created - never any other - and
' verify it by a live enumeration of open documents: before the close, the
' title must identify exactly our object among open documents (an empty
' title is refused); after it, no open document may answer to the title.
' A failed query proves nothing and leaves the run failed. Every call is
' captured at its own named stage and recorded. The owner rule: runs
' leave no documents open.
Sub CloseOwnedDoc(ByRef closedOk As Boolean)
    Dim exact As String
    Dim cnt As Long
    Dim isOurs As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    closedOk = False
    If swDoc Is Nothing Then
        closedOk = True
        WriteLine LineFor("close-owned-document", 0, "", "no owned document to close")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    Err.Clear
    exact = swDoc.GetTitle
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("close-owned-document", n, d, "stage=title")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Sub
    If Trim(exact) = "" Then
        WriteLine LineFor("close-owned-document", -1, "empty title", "refusing to close: an empty title would target the active document")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    If Not DocEnumeration(exact, cnt, isOurs) Then
        WriteLine LineFor("close-owned-document", -1, "enumeration failed", "refusing to close: the open-document query failed")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    If cnt <> 1 Or Not isOurs Then
        WriteLine LineFor("close-owned-document", -1, "matches=" & Trim(Str(cnt)) & " ours=" & CStr(isOurs), "refusing to close: the title does not identify exactly our document")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    Err.Clear
    swApp.CloseDoc exact
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("close-owned-document", n, d, "stage=closedoc " & exact)
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Sub
    If Not DocEnumeration(exact, cnt, isOurs) Then
        WriteLine LineFor("close-owned-document", -1, "enumeration failed", "closure NOT verified: the open-document query failed")
        Exit Sub
    End If
    If cnt = 0 Then
        closedOk = True
        WriteLine LineFor("close-owned-document", 0, "", "verified closed: no open document answers to " & exact)
    Else
        WriteLine LineFor("close-owned-document", -1, "matches=" & Trim(Str(cnt)), "closure NOT verified: an open document still answers to the title")
    End If
End Sub

' The keep-mode handoff must be a live, nonempty, uniquely owned
' document: the title must be nonempty and a complete enumeration must
' find exactly one match, ours. False = the handoff is unverified and
' the document is never reported as retained.
Function OwnedHandoffVerified(ByVal tag As String, ByRef titleOut As String) As Boolean
    Dim cnt As Long
    Dim isOurs As Boolean
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    OwnedHandoffVerified = False
    titleOut = ""
    Err.Clear
    titleOut = swDoc.GetTitle
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("handoff-" & tag, n, d, "stage=title")
    If n <> 0 Then Exit Function
    If Trim(titleOut) = "" Then
        WriteLine LineFor("handoff-" & tag, -1, "empty title", "handoff NOT verified")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If Not DocEnumeration(titleOut, cnt, isOurs) Then
        WriteLine LineFor("handoff-" & tag, -1, "enumeration failed", "handoff NOT verified")
        Exit Function
    End If
    If cnt = 1 And isOurs Then
        WriteLine LineFor("handoff-" & tag, 0, "", "verified live and owned: " & titleOut)
        OwnedHandoffVerified = True
    Else
        WriteLine LineFor("handoff-" & tag, -1, "matches=" & Trim(Str(cnt)) & " ours=" & CStr(isOurs), "handoff NOT verified")
    End If
End Function

' The proven minimal.swb helper, retained at the task's helper list; the
' keep report uses the VERIFIED handoffTitle instead of this second
' query. Its own API call is captured and recorded.
Function OwnedDocTitle() As String
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    On Error Resume Next
    OwnedDocTitle = ""
    If swDoc Is Nothing Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    OwnedDocTitle = "" & swDoc.GetTitle
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    WriteLine LineFor("owned-doc-title", n, d, "title=" & OwnedDocTitle)
End Function

' The first feature type names in the tree, with any captured walk error
' embedded in the text: the report names what the scan actually saw when
' plane selection fails.
Function TreeSummary() As String
    Dim feat As SldWorks.Feature
    Dim s As String
    Dim planes As String
    Dim errs As String
    Dim nm As String
    Dim fn As String
    Dim i As Long
    Dim n As Long
    Dim d As String
    Dim n2 As Long
    Dim d2 As String
    On Error Resume Next
    Err.Clear
    Set feat = swDoc.FirstFeature
    n = Err.Number
    d = Err.Description
    If n <> 0 Then errs = errs & "firstfeature err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
    Do While Not feat Is Nothing And i < 300
        Err.Clear
        nm = feat.GetTypeName2()
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        If n <> 0 Then errs = errs & "typename err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
        If n = 0 Then
            If InStr(1, nm, "lane", vbTextCompare) > 0 Then
                Err.Clear
                fn = feat.Name
                n2 = Err.Number
                d2 = Err.Description
                If n2 <> 0 Then
                    errs = errs & "name err=" & Trim(Str(n2)) & " " & d2 & "; "
                Else
                    planes = planes & nm & "/" & fn & " "
                End If
            End If
            If i < 10 Then s = s & nm & " "
        End If
        i = i + 1
        Err.Clear
        Set feat = feat.GetNextFeature
        n = Err.Number
        d = Err.Description
        If n <> 0 Then errs = errs & "nextfeature err=" & Trim(Str(n)) & " " & d & "; "
    Loop
    TreeSummary = Trim(Str(i)) & " features; plane-like: [" & Trim(planes) & "]; first: " & s & "; walk-errs: " & errs
End Function

' The report path travels in a one-line file under the TEMP directory that
' the host rewrites before every run: preferred over CRAFT_BRIDGE_REPORT,
' because the macro runs inside the SolidWorks process, which may be an
' instance that started long ago with a stale environment. The environment
' variable is only the fallback for when the path file is missing or blank.
' Host-file plumbing: it suppresses its own I/O errors by design and is
' outside the per-call SolidWorks API evidence contract.
Function ReportPathFromHost() As String
    Dim p As String
    Dim f As Integer
    Dim oneLine As String
    Dim got As Boolean
    ReportPathFromHost = ""
    On Error Resume Next
    p = Environ$("TEMP")
    If p <> "" Then
        p = p & "\craft-bridge-report-path.txt"
        Err.Clear
        f = FreeFile
        Open p For Input As #f
        If Err.Number = 0 Then
            Err.Clear
            Line Input #f, oneLine
            got = (Err.Number = 0)
            Err.Clear
            Close #f
            If got Then
                oneLine = Trim(oneLine)
                If oneLine <> "" Then
                    ReportPathFromHost = oneLine
                    Exit Function
                End If
            End If
        End If
        Err.Clear
    End If
    ReportPathFromHost = Trim(Environ$("CRAFT_BRIDGE_REPORT"))
End Function

' Truncate the report so this run never inherits a previous run's lines.
' Host-file plumbing, as above.
Sub StartReport()
    On Error Resume Next
    Dim f As Integer
    f = FreeFile
    Open reportPath For Output As #f
    Close #f
End Sub

' One line, one fresh handle: open, print, close. Nothing to leak, nothing
' to collide with. Host-file plumbing, as above.
Sub WriteLine(ByVal text As String)
    On Error Resume Next
    Dim f As Integer
    f = FreeFile
    Open reportPath For Append As #f
    Print #f, text
    Close #f
End Sub

Sub WriteStep(ByVal idx As Long, ByVal command As String, ByVal status As String, ByVal message As String)
    WriteLine "{""type"":""step"",""index"":" & Trim(Str(idx)) & ",""command"":""" & JsonStr(command) & """,""status"":""" & JsonStr(status) & """,""message"":""" & JsonStr(message) & """}"
End Sub

' JSON string escaping. This is not VBA-literal escaping: it is only for the
' report file. Generated code strings are escaped separately by the generator.
Function JsonStr(ByVal s As String) As String
    Dim t As String
    t = Replace(s, "\", "\\")
    t = Replace(t, """", "\""")
    t = Replace(t, vbCrLf, "\n")
    t = Replace(t, vbCr, "\n")
    t = Replace(t, vbLf, "\n")
    t = Replace(t, vbTab, "\t")
    JsonStr = t
End Function

' Cleanup authorization from the host's path file: "close" (third line
' reads close-after-run), "keep" (a two-line file) or "unknown". Host-
' file plumbing, as above.
Function CloseMode() As String
    Dim p As String
    Dim f As Integer
    Dim oneLine As String
    Dim ok As Boolean
    Dim e3 As Long
    CloseMode = "unknown"
    On Error Resume Next
    p = Environ$("TEMP")
    If p = "" Then Exit Function
    p = p & "\craft-bridge-report-path.txt"
    Err.Clear
    f = FreeFile
    Open p For Input As #f
    If Err.Number <> 0 Then Exit Function
    Err.Clear
    Line Input #f, oneLine
    ok = (Err.Number = 0)
    Err.Clear
    If ok Then Line Input #f, oneLine
    ok = ok And (Err.Number = 0)
    Err.Clear
    If ok Then Line Input #f, oneLine
    e3 = Err.Number
    Close #f
    If Not ok Then Exit Function
    If e3 = 0 Then
        If Trim(oneLine) = "close-after-run" Then CloseMode = "close" Else CloseMode = "unknown"
    ElseIf e3 = 62 And ok Then
        CloseMode = "keep"
    End If
End Function
